  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Reduction of and Improved Operational Response to Gender-Based Violence through Camp Management and Site Planning Phase VIII</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since 2015, IOM has been implementing a global project on Gender-Based Violence (GBV) prevention and risk mitigation under the Safe from the Start Initiative (SftS) supported by the US Bureau of Population, Refugees and Migration. IOM&apos;s Global SftS project is now entering its eighth year. IOM continues to pursue key milestones set against commitments made by IOM under the 2021-2025 Roadmap of the Global Call to Action on Protection against GBV in emergencies including: to strengthen risk mitigation and response capacities in key technical areas where IOM brings a strategic added-value to collective efforts on GBV - including camp coordination and camp management, shelter and settlements, water, sanitation and hygiene, and health; to pursue the institutionalization and operationalization of the GBV in Crises Framework to foster more coherent and holistic responses to GBV in emergencies; and to continue supporting inter-agency initiatives from the Inter-Agency Standing Committee and UN-wide system on collective protection from sexual exploitation and abuse. IOM is further exploring how the SftS initiative can contribute to build a stronger understanding and response to gendered impact of climate displacement.</narrative>
  </description>
